{%- comment -%}
  Turns tab-separated text into a normalised row string and OUTPUTS it.

  In:  raw    the pasted text
  Out: prints rows joined by "~~", cells joined by "||"

  Callers capture the output and derive their own counts:

    {%- capture sc_rows -%}{%- render 'size-chart-parse', raw: raw -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign sc_row_list = sc_rows | strip | split: '~~' -%}

  This prints rather than assigning because Shopify forbids {% include %}
  inside a snippet rendered with {% render %}, and {% render %} cannot
  assign back to its caller. Printing plus capture is the only shape that
  keeps one parser and keeps every consumer isolated.

  Rows shorter than the widest row are padded, so a ragged paste cannot
  shift cells into the wrong column.

  Carriage returns from Windows Excel are removed by the per-cell `strip`:
  a CR only ever lands at the end of a cell.

  The blob is deliberately NOT stripped before splitting. A grid pasted from a
  spreadsheet starts with an empty corner cell, so its first line begins with a
  tab — and stripping the blob ate that tab, which shifted every column heading
  one place left and put each one over the wrong column.

  Rows whose cells are all empty except the first are dropped. A spreadsheet
  carries an axis caption ("Height (cm)") and a title on their own rows, and
  rendering those as data put empty rows through the middle of the table.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign sc_tab = '	' -%}
{%- assign sc_lines = raw | split: '
' -%}

{%- assign sc_cols_count = 0 -%}
{%- for line in sc_lines -%}
  {%- assign cells = line | split: sc_tab -%}
  {%- if cells.size > sc_cols_count -%}
    {%- assign sc_cols_count = cells.size -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- assign sc_rows = '' -%}
{%- assign sc_rows_count = 0 -%}
{%- for line in sc_lines -%}
  {%- assign trimmed = line | strip -%}
  {%- if trimmed == blank -%}
    {%- continue -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign cells = line | split: sc_tab -%}

  {%- comment -%} A caption or title row: a label and nothing beside it. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign has_data = false -%}
  {%- for cell in cells offset: 1 -%}
    {%- assign c = cell | strip -%}
    {%- if c != '' -%}
      {%- assign has_data = true -%}
      {%- break -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- unless has_data -%}
    {%- continue -%}
  {%- endunless -%}

  {%- assign row = '' -%}
  {%- for i in (1..sc_cols_count) -%}
    {%- assign idx = forloop.index0 -%}
    {%- assign cell = cells[idx] | default: '' | strip -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}
      {%- assign row = cell -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign row = row | append: '||' | append: cell -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if sc_rows_count == 0 -%}
    {%- assign sc_rows = row -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign sc_rows = sc_rows | append: '~~' | append: row -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign sc_rows_count = sc_rows_count | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- sc_rows -}}
